1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:01,800
He can see the future.

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:03,450
Every war.

3
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:04,850
Every betrayal.

4
00:00:05,420 --> 00:00:07,870
Every road that leads
away from this throne.

5
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:12,050
And on every one of those
roads, the galaxy burns.

6
00:00:12,850 --> 00:00:15,500
Twelve years ago, Paul Atreides
won everything.

7
00:00:16,130 --> 00:00:19,060
Now sixty-one billion people
are dead in his name,

8
00:00:19,210 --> 00:00:23,240
and four of the most powerful forces
in the universe have joined together

9
00:00:23,090 --> 00:00:24,280
to destroy him.

10
00:00:24,130 --> 00:00:27,410
Their weapon is not an army.

11
00:00:27,810 --> 00:00:28,760
It is a gift.

12
00:00:29,310 --> 00:00:31,400
A dead man, brought back to life.

13
00:00:31,990 --> 00:00:33,380
And Paul can see the trap.

14
00:00:33,780 --> 00:00:35,470
He is going to walk into it anyway.

15
00:00:36,070 --> 00:00:37,880
This is the story of Dune Messiah.

16
00:00:38,350 --> 00:00:40,900
The fall of the man who became a god.

17
00:00:49,270 --> 00:00:53,940
Twelve years after his victory, Paul Atreides
rules the known universe from

18
00:00:53,790 --> 00:00:56,900
a citadel of stone on the
desert planet Arrakis.

19
00:00:57,300 --> 00:01:00,150
To the Fremen of the desert,
he is Muad'Dib.

20
00:01:00,550 --> 00:01:03,720
To billions of pilgrims,
he is something more.

21
00:01:04,430 --> 00:01:07,000
They cross the stars to stand
beneath his windows,

22
00:01:07,210 --> 00:01:08,620
and they call him a god.

23
00:01:09,020 --> 00:01:11,530
His power rests on one substance.

24
00:01:12,060 --> 00:01:12,910
The spice.

25
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:17,530
The Spacing Guild cannot
fold space without it.

26
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:20,800
The great houses cannot live without it.

27
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,290
And Paul has shown that he can destroy it.

28
00:01:25,080 --> 00:01:28,710
To seal his victory, he married
the Princess Irulan,

29
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:31,230
daughter of the emperor he overthrew.

30
00:01:31,940 --> 00:01:33,690
It is a marriage of politics.

31
00:01:34,180 --> 00:01:35,230
Never of love.

32
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:40,490
His heart belongs to Chani, the Fremen
woman who stood beside him in the

33
00:01:40,340 --> 00:01:40,810
desert.

34
00:01:41,580 --> 00:01:46,370
She is his concubine in name, and
his true wife in everything else.

35
00:01:47,460 --> 00:01:52,210
But long before he took the throne,
Paul saw something in the future.

36
00:01:52,820 --> 00:01:56,970
A holy war, carried across
the stars in his name.

37
00:01:57,820 --> 00:01:59,470
He tried to stop it.

38
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:00,770
He could not.

39
00:02:03,370 --> 00:02:06,440
The jihad swept out from
Arrakis on Guild ships,

40
00:02:06,530 --> 00:02:09,580
and for twelve years, the
Fremen legions marched.

41
00:02:10,330 --> 00:02:13,580
One night, Paul does the arithmetic
of his own reign.

42
00:02:14,190 --> 00:02:15,840
Sixty-one billion dead.

43
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:18,090
Ninety planets sterilized.

44
00:02:18,490 --> 00:02:21,240
Five hundred more, utterly demoralized.

45
00:02:21,650 --> 00:02:25,150
He measures himself against the
tyrants of ancient history,

46
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,690
and finds them small.

47
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:30,110
Around his name, a priesthood rises.

48
00:02:30,540 --> 00:02:31,310
The Qizarate.

49
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:34,410
Its priests build temples, sell his image,

50
00:02:34,460 --> 00:02:37,630
and turn the faith of the desert
into the religion of an empire.

51
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:41,450
Among its leaders is Korba,
once a Fedaykin warrior,

52
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:42,410
now a priest.

53
00:02:43,180 --> 00:02:45,310
And the Fremen themselves are changing.

54
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:50,230
Warriors who once saved every drop of
water now watch it spill from palace

55
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:50,890
fountains.

56
00:02:51,560 --> 00:02:52,930
Paul sees all of it.

57
00:02:53,330 --> 00:02:55,040
And he sees something worse.

58
00:02:55,670 --> 00:02:59,600
Even if he died tomorrow,
the jihad would not stop.

59
00:03:00,130 --> 00:03:02,520
His legend would keep killing without him.

60
00:03:02,920 --> 00:03:06,310
Every path he can see leads
somewhere terrible.

61
00:03:06,960 --> 00:03:10,430
And on the narrowest of them,
someone is already waiting.

62
00:03:11,630 --> 00:03:13,700
Before we step into that room.

63
00:03:14,410 --> 00:03:17,400
If you love the hidden
histories of Arrakis,

64
00:03:17,790 --> 00:03:21,480
Westeros and Middle-earth, subscribe
to the Mythic Archives,

65
00:03:21,330 --> 00:03:24,680
and tap the bell, so you
never miss a record.

66
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:31,550
On Wallach Nine, the cold home
world of the Bene Gesserit,

67
00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:34,470
four enemies of Muad'Dib meet in secret.

68
00:03:35,160 --> 00:03:39,650
The first is the Bene Gesserit, an ancient
sisterhood that has spent generations

69
00:03:39,500 --> 00:03:43,970
breeding human bloodlines, searching
for a messiah they could control.

70
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:48,110
Their envoy is the Reverend
Mother Gaius Helen Mohiam.

71
00:03:48,640 --> 00:03:53,150
Years ago, she held a poisoned needle
to a boy's neck to test whether he

72
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:53,690
was human.

73
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:55,490
That boy was Paul.

74
00:03:56,110 --> 00:03:59,830
The second is the Spacing Guild,
represented by Edric,

75
00:03:59,960 --> 00:04:03,190
a Navigator who floats in a
tank of orange spice gas.

76
00:04:03,720 --> 00:04:06,790
His presence hides the plotters
from Paul's prescience,

77
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:08,730
like a shadow in his visions.

78
00:04:09,420 --> 00:04:13,210
The third is the Bene Tleilax,
masters of flesh and genetics.

79
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:18,010
Their envoy is Scytale, a Face
Dancer, who can become anyone.

80
00:04:18,740 --> 00:04:21,490
And the fourth sits inside
the palace itself.

81
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:25,650
Princess Irulan, the wife
Paul will never love.

82
00:04:26,050 --> 00:04:30,400
In secret, she has been hiding a
contraceptive in Chani's food,

83
00:04:30,610 --> 00:04:33,580
so that Chani can never give Paul an heir.

84
00:04:34,290 --> 00:04:36,120
None of them can simply kill him.

85
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:38,050
He would see it coming.

86
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:41,370
And a dead Muad'Dib would become a martyr,

87
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:43,810
more powerful than a living one.

88
00:04:44,220 --> 00:04:46,390
So they will not attack the emperor.

89
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:48,490
They will break the man.

90
00:04:51,090 --> 00:04:54,940
The conspirators come to Arrakeen
bearing a gift for the emperor.

91
00:04:55,410 --> 00:04:58,080
From behind a veil steps a man Paul knows.

92
00:04:58,570 --> 00:05:00,160
A man who died for him.

93
00:05:00,970 --> 00:05:01,600
Duncan Idaho.

94
00:05:02,210 --> 00:05:04,060
Swordmaster of House Atreides.

95
00:05:04,670 --> 00:05:07,680
Killed years ago, fighting
to cover Paul's escape.

96
00:05:08,450 --> 00:05:12,940
The Tleilaxu have grown a new body
from his dead cells in their vats.

97
00:05:13,340 --> 00:05:14,030
A ghola.

98
00:05:14,430 --> 00:05:15,620
They call him Hayt.

99
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:18,250
He has no memory of his past life.

100
00:05:18,100 --> 00:05:21,340
His eyes are polished Tleilaxu metal.

101
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:26,560
And he has been trained as a Mentat, a
human mind that thinks like a computer.

102
00:05:27,390 --> 00:05:29,560
Paul knows a weapon when he sees one.

103
00:05:29,960 --> 00:05:33,090
But refusing the gift would
be its own kind of defeat.

104
00:05:33,520 --> 00:05:34,850
So he accepts it.

105
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:37,970
Hayt becomes his companion, his advisor,

106
00:05:38,360 --> 00:05:41,910
the one voice in the citadel unafraid
to tell him the truth.

107
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:46,650
But deep inside that new mind, the
Tleilaxu have buried a command.

108
00:05:47,070 --> 00:05:50,210
A single trigger, waiting
for the right moment.

109
00:05:50,610 --> 00:05:51,600
And remember this.

110
00:05:52,090 --> 00:05:55,260
If the Tleilaxu can bring
back one dead man,

111
00:05:55,690 --> 00:05:57,000
they can bring back another.

112
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:01,850
Even among the Fremen, there are traitors.

113
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:05,210
Old naibs and priests
have joined the plot.

114
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:09,050
One evening, a young Fremen woman
arrives at the citadel.

115
00:06:09,520 --> 00:06:11,990
Her name is Lichna, daughter of Otheym,

116
00:06:12,180 --> 00:06:13,910
one of Paul's old Fedaykin.

117
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:19,350
Her father is dying, she says, and wants
to see the emperor one last time.

118
00:06:20,140 --> 00:06:21,810
But the girl is not Lichna.

119
00:06:22,220 --> 00:06:24,410
It is Scytale, wearing her face.

120
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:29,450
Paul goes anyway, at night, on foot,
through the streets of Arrakeen.

121
00:06:30,060 --> 00:06:33,430
Otheym lies dying in a small
house in the poor quarter.

122
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,730
His final gift is strange.

123
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:41,290
A dwarf named Bijaz, a living recorder
who carries in his memory the names

124
00:06:41,140 --> 00:06:42,250
of every traitor.

125
00:06:43,180 --> 00:06:46,750
Then, in the street outside,
the trap is sprung.

126
00:06:47,180 --> 00:06:48,230
A stone burner.

127
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:51,250
An atomic weapon, made for one purpose.

128
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:52,170
Light.

129
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:54,550
Paul survives.

130
00:06:55,350 --> 00:06:56,700
His eyes do not.

131
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:02,950
Among the Fremen, the law
is ancient and merciless.

132
00:07:03,520 --> 00:07:07,310
The blind are taken into the desert,
and left to Shai-Hulud.

133
00:07:08,080 --> 00:07:09,810
Paul breaks that law.

134
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:15,010
He orders Tleilaxu eyes for every
soldier blinded beside him.

135
00:07:16,300 --> 00:07:18,430
And then, the impossible.

136
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:21,830
The blind emperor walks into his court,

137
00:07:22,140 --> 00:07:25,270
finds every face, and answers
every question,

138
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:27,580
as if nothing has happened.

139
00:07:27,430 --> 00:07:33,180
He is seeing through his visions, moving
through a future he has already

140
00:07:33,030 --> 00:07:33,920
memorized.

141
00:07:34,630 --> 00:07:36,640
The Fremen call it a miracle.

142
00:07:37,270 --> 00:07:41,420
For Paul, it is the loneliest
kind of sight.

143
00:07:42,450 --> 00:07:47,540
And somewhere ahead, the vision has
an ending he cannot see past.

144
00:07:50,140 --> 00:07:52,210
Chani is pregnant at last.

145
00:07:52,820 --> 00:07:57,090
But years of Irulan's hidden contraceptive
have weakened her body,

146
00:07:57,380 --> 00:08:00,370
and the pregnancy is racing
out of control.

147
00:08:01,240 --> 00:08:06,710
She travels to Sietch Tabr, the desert
stronghold where she and Paul first

148
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:08,610
found each other, to give birth.

149
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:11,810
Paul waits outside the birth chamber.

150
00:08:12,210 --> 00:08:14,180
He already knows what is coming.

151
00:08:14,730 --> 00:08:15,080
Twins.

152
00:08:15,870 --> 00:08:17,780
A son, and a daughter.

153
00:08:18,270 --> 00:08:19,760
Leto and Ghanima.

154
00:08:20,330 --> 00:08:21,580
And Chani dies.

155
00:08:24,730 --> 00:08:26,360
Paul's grief is total.

156
00:08:26,990 --> 00:08:29,540
And in that moment, his vision breaks.

157
00:08:30,390 --> 00:08:34,060
In every vision, he had
seen only a daughter.

158
00:08:34,890 --> 00:08:37,080
He had never seen his son.

159
00:08:39,680 --> 00:08:41,690
Now the hidden command awakens.

160
00:08:42,160 --> 00:08:43,630
Hayt turns on the emperor.

161
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:46,890
But the conflict inside him is too great.

162
00:08:47,420 --> 00:08:51,910
The ghola's mind breaks open, and
Duncan Idaho remembers who he is.

163
00:08:52,920 --> 00:08:54,750
Then Scytale makes his offer.

164
00:08:55,460 --> 00:08:58,910
The Tleilaxu can bring
Chani back, as a ghola,

165
00:08:59,100 --> 00:09:00,630
just as they brought back Duncan.

166
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:03,830
The price is everything Paul holds.

167
00:09:04,060 --> 00:09:08,170
And to force the choice, Scytale
threatens the newborn twins.

168
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:10,830
Paul is blind.

169
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:12,830
But he is not alone.

170
00:09:14,060 --> 00:09:17,730
Through the eyes of his newborn
son, he sees the room.

171
00:09:18,240 --> 00:09:20,290
And he throws his crysknife.

172
00:09:21,060 --> 00:09:22,050
Scytale falls.

173
00:09:24,650 --> 00:09:28,440
Now truly blind, with no
vision left to guide him,

174
00:09:28,990 --> 00:09:30,800
Paul chooses the way of the Fremen.

175
00:09:31,450 --> 00:09:34,420
He walks out into the deep desert, alone.

176
00:09:34,950 --> 00:09:36,620
The wind takes his footprints.

177
00:09:37,250 --> 00:09:39,940
Somewhere out there, the
great worms are moving.

178
00:09:40,530 --> 00:09:41,900
There is no grave.

179
00:09:42,300 --> 00:09:43,470
There is no body.

180
00:09:43,870 --> 00:09:44,980
The man is gone.

181
00:09:47,430 --> 00:09:50,200
Behind him, the empire goes on.

182
00:09:50,810 --> 00:09:53,860
His sister Alia rules as
regent for the twins.

183
00:09:54,530 --> 00:09:58,360
Duncan Idaho, restored,
stands at her side.

184
00:09:58,790 --> 00:10:04,480
And Irulan, the wife who betrayed him, swears
her life to raising his children.

185
00:10:07,080 --> 00:10:10,790
Muad'Dib wanted to save humanity
from a terrible future.

186
00:10:11,300 --> 00:10:13,990
Instead, he became what he feared most.

187
00:10:14,740 --> 00:10:18,210
A god whose name was used
to justify slaughter.

188
00:10:19,580 --> 00:10:22,470
That is the warning buried in this story.

189
00:10:23,660 --> 00:10:24,830
Beware of heroes.

190
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:28,270
Beware of anyone the crowd
is ready to worship.

191
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:31,150
But the desert keeps its secrets.

192
00:10:31,940 --> 00:10:35,630
Years from now, a blind preacher
will walk out of the sand,

193
00:10:35,920 --> 00:10:38,410
speaking against the religion of Muad'Dib.

194
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:43,730
And a boy named Leto will begin to
see a path no one else can see.

195
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:48,730
A golden path, three and a
half thousand years long.

196
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:52,150
That is the next record in the archive.

197
00:10:53,550 --> 00:10:58,960
So, was Paul Atreides a hero, or
the greatest tyrant in history?

198
00:10:59,870 --> 00:11:01,880
Tell us what you think in the comments.

199
00:11:02,410 --> 00:11:05,900
If this story stayed with you,
give the video a like,

200
00:11:05,750 --> 00:11:08,060
and subscribe to the Mythic Archives.

201
00:11:08,610 --> 00:11:10,680
The archive is always open.
